WEBVTT

00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:20,150
Doing keto, it's tempting to buy plant-based dairy products to take the place of real dairy, such as cream cheese, cheese, yogurt, etc.

00:00:20,150 --> 00:00:31,350
But looking at these ingredients in these plant-based substitutes, they look a little bit like fracon foods, isolates, gums, etc.

00:00:31,350 --> 00:00:38,350
Is it better to void these altogether or are all these additives relatively harmless?

00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:51,350
Well, I would say some are relatively harmless, some of the gums and some of the other different substitutes that they use.

00:00:51,350 --> 00:01:04,350
You can develop antibodies again so that you could have sensitivities to it, but some of the fibers and stuff that they use are relatively harmless.

00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:15,350
You'd have to look up each ingredient. Obviously, it's much better to eat real dairy or, you know, but we're trying to stay up, you're on a dairy-free diet, you can't do that.

00:01:15,350 --> 00:01:19,350
So just stay away from some of those things are probably the best.

00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:26,350
As far as yogurt, like there's coconut milk, yogurt's out there that I think are just fine.

00:01:27,350 --> 00:01:36,350
You know, most of the dairy yogurt that you find out there, unless you're getting it organic, is got a bunch of additives and garbage.

00:01:36,350 --> 00:01:48,350
Most of the dairy products, unless you're getting it clean, dairy, clean organic or from the farm or something like that, it's going to have a bunch of garbage in it as well.

00:01:48,350 --> 00:01:58,350
So just because it's dairy doesn't mean that it's necessarily going to be good for us either.

00:01:58,350 --> 00:02:08,350
So there's a lot of nasty stuff even in what we would term as real food as well.

